---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CommitMessageGenerator from '../../components/CommitMessageGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI Commit Message Generator"
  description="Paste a git diff and generate a clear commit message — Conventional Commits or plain English. Bring your own Anthropic API key."
>
  <CommitMessageGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why use AI for commit messages</h2>
  <p>
    Writing a clear, specific commit message takes a moment of context
    switching away from the code you just wrote. This tool reads your diff
    and drafts a message for you to review and use — you stay in control of
    what actually gets committed.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Get a free Anthropic API key at console.anthropic.com (new accounts get free credits).</li>
    <li>Paste it in the field above — it's stored only in your browser, never on our servers.</li>
    <li>Paste your <code>git diff</code> output.</li>
    <li>Pick a style and generate.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>AI Commit Message FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why do I need my own API key?</strong> This keeps the tool free
    to use with no rate limits imposed by us — you pay Anthropic directly
    for what you use, typically fractions of a cent per commit message.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Is my code sent anywhere besides Anthropic?</strong> No — your
    diff is proxied directly to Anthropic's API using your key and is not
    logged or stored by this tool.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
